    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24405" root="صف" body-key="S">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَفْصَفَ</span></b>  <i>He journeyed,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَارَ</span>, O, and
so in copies of the K,) or <i>became,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَارَ</span>, so in the
CK,) <i>alone in a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَفْصَف</span>, or <i>level tract of land.</i>
(O, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <i>He pastured upon the trees
called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَفْصَاف</span>. (O, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَفْصَفَةٌ</span> [as an
inf. n., or as a simple subst.,] signifies The <i>crying</i>
or <i>cry,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَوْت</span>,) of the sparrow, which is called
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صُفْصُف</span> (O, K) in some one or more of the
dialects. (O.)

